==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Münster, Prinzipalmarkt, Arkaden -- 2021 -- 8931-3.jpg|An '''alley''' in {{w|Münster}}, Germany|thumb]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæ.li/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-alley.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æli|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|aley}}, from {{der|en|fro|alee}}, feminine of {{m|fro|alé}}, past participle of {{m|fro|aler||to go}} (French {{m|fr|aller}}). {{doublet|en|allée}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A narrow [[street]] or [[passageway]], especially one through the middle of a block giving access to the rear of lots of buildings.
#: {{syn|en|alleyway|Thesaurus:alley}}
#: {{ux|en|The parking lot to my friend's apartment building is in the '''alley'''.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The area between the [[outfielder]]s.
#: {{syn|en|gap}}
#: {{ux|en|He hit one deep into the '''alley'''.}}
# {{lb|en|bowling}} An establishment where bowling is played.
#: {{syn|en|bowling alley}}
# {{lb|en|bowling}} An elongated wooden strip of floor along which a [[bowling ball]] is rolled.
#: {{syn|en|lane}}
# {{lb|en|tennis}} The extra area between the sidelines or [[tramline]]s on a [[tennis court]] that is used for doubles matches.
# {{senseid|en|allée}} A walk or passage in a garden or park, bordered by rows of trees or bushes.
#* {{RQ:Milton Comus|passage=I know each lane and every '''alley''' green.}}
# A passageway between rows of [[pew]]s in a [[church]].
# {{lb|en|perspective drawing}} Any passage having the entrance represented as wider than the exit, so as to give the appearance of length.
# The space between two rows of [[compositor]]s' [[stand]]s in a [[print]]ing office.
# {{lb|en|informal|rare}} A [[group]] of [[clown]]s; {{non-gloss definition|the [[collective noun]] for clowns.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Charles William Jefford|title=Academia Nuts|page=78
|passage={{...}} '''alley''' of clowns had sprung like a fungus growth from the dung heap of the First World War.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2021|author=T. K. Wrathbone|title=All Clowns Must Die!
|passage=“{{...}} Something must've happened to him when he was little.”<br>“Which would give him a reason to hate them,” Oliver replied and was pushed aside by an '''alley''' of clowns. “Hey!”<br>“Sorry, kid. Didn't see you there,” one clown called over.}}

